    "result_text": "All remaining matches are intentional (doc comments referencing the former fields, and the new `luhnCheckDigit` helper name). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. All 68 tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nChanges made:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the `customer_code` column/field and its accessors with `member_id` / `getMemberId` / `setMemberId`.\n\n- **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 `saveOwner` now stamps a `memberId` on new owners. Renamed the generator to `generateMemberId`, which builds `REGION + FY(2-digit) + HASH8 + CHK`, where:\n  - `REGION` is the existing postcode-then-city derivation,\n  - `FY` is the 2-digit fiscal year of the registration date (new `fiscalYear2` helper, fiscal year starting 1 July),\n  - `HASH8` is the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex used by the region-and-hash identity,\n  - `CHK` is a Luhn digit over the digits of `REGION+FY+HASH8` (new `luhnCheckDigit` helper).\n  - Collision de-duplication now applies to `memberId` (`deduplicateMemberId`).\n\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and methods; `memberId` now auto-maps from the stored field; `locality` (which feeds `ownerSegment`) now derives the region from the `memberId`'s leading-letters segment; `fiscalYear` retained.\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 audit line now logs `id`, `memberId`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel` (dropped `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`); `primaryIdentifier` returns `memberId`; the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event carries `memberId`.\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId` property (regenerates the DTO).\n\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id`.",
